=== Old Dynamic System and Project Alloy ===
The drop chance was previously believed to be handled by a dynamic system. It was intended to have a base drop chance of {{Chance|0.000125%|1|800,000|runs}}. This drop chance would apply in all [[Crystal Hollows]] lobbies. Every hour ({{Green|3}} [[SkyBlock Time|SkyBlock days]]), this chance would be multiplied by {{Green|10}}, capping at {{Green|×100}}, or {{Chance|0.0125%|1|8,000|runs}}. Once a player obtained a '''Divan's Alloy''', this chance would be reset, and the cycle would repeat. Additionally, it would only roll once per bundle unlike all the other loot.
*This system did indeed exist in the game's code, which is where the information on the official wiki page came from. However, it was never actually in effect, as the drop chance was overwritten to be {{Chance|0.1%|1|1,000|runs}} elsewhere.
**Prior to the official wiki acknowledging the discrepancy, a player-made research group called [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1as6zCMxQMQKE43MP60ToI9K14WUbQz47C5AZbNGIym0/edit#gid=0 Project Alloy] had already discovered it. The research noted that most drops occurred within the first few hours after a previous drop, which means that the dynamic drop system was never in effect. It was also discovered that even the highest claimed drop chance of {{Chance|0.0125%|1|8,000|runs}} was statistically impossible given their data that suggested an average of {{Chance|0.0778%|1|1,285|runs}}.
*A command called {{Code|/resetdivanchance}} was also visible to players. This was likely intended to be used by staff to manually reset the drop chance of the '''Divan's Alloy'''.
*The player was required to have at least {{green|25}} hours of playtime to drop a '''Divan's Alloy'''.

